  "record_bodies_before": {
    "courier-relay/cross-account-delivery-identity": "Courier Relay: delivery identity and acceptance-rule contract across protocol versions (identity established for trial-ewy on protocol \"1\"; acceptance rule revised for trial-tfh with permanent adoption of protocol \"2\" as current; \"accepted\" command added for trial-tau on protocol \"2\" only; \"accepted\" extended for trial-hjc to also support explicit protocol \"1\").\n\nIdentity (unchanged by protocol version):\n- Protocol \"1\" identity (used by \"count\" and by \"accepted\" when protocol \"1\" is explicit): delivery_id ALONE identifies a delivery across all accounts -- the same delivery_id under a different account_id is still the SAME delivery, per the providers original delivery-ID allocation guarantee (vendor/protocol-1.md). This is the original provider contract that shipped with the initial \"count\" issue (trial-adg).\n- Protocol \"2\" identity (used by \"summary\", and by \"accepted\" for protocol \"2\"/omitted): the pair (account_id, delivery_id) identifies a delivery -- the same delivery_id under a different account_id is a SEPARATE delivery. This is the newer contract from trial-tfh/trial-ewy.\n- The single-account \"count\" command is unaffected by this distinction in practice since it only ever sees one accounts receipts; its delivery_id-alone dedupe is a code-simplicity choice for count, not evidence against the protocol-1 cross-account identity rule.\n\nAcceptance rule, protocol \"1\" (still explicitly supported, no longer current): within one identity group, the accepted receipt is the one with the EARLIEST occurred_at (compared as a UTC instant); ties broken by the lexicographically (Unicode code-point) smallest record_id. All other receipts in the group are duplicates.\n\nAcceptance rule, protocol \"2\" (current as of trial-tfh; provider permanently adopted this contract, approved by the integration owner): within one identity group, the accepted receipt is the one with the LATEST occurred_at (UTC instant); ties still broken by smallest record_id. All other receipts in the group are duplicates.\n\nProtocol selection: an omitted \"protocol\" field selects the current protocol (now \"2\"). Explicit \"protocol\":\"1\" or \"protocol\":\"2\" selects that versions rule set for \"count\" and \"summary\"; both remain supported. accepted_count = number of distinct identity-group keys present; duplicate_count = total receipts - accepted_count. Empty batch -> 0/0.\n\n\"accepted\" command (added trial-tau for protocol \"2\" only; extended trial-hjc to add protocol \"1\"): ACCEPTED_SUPPORTED_PROTOCOLS is now {\"1\",\"2\"} (previously {\"2\"} only) -- an explicit \"protocol\":\"1\" request is accepted, not {\"error\":\"unknown_command\"}. The command selects its identity key function AND its earliest/latest-wins rule together based on the requested protocol: protocol \"1\" uses the protocol-1 identity (delivery_id alone) with earliest-wins/smallest-record_id-tie-break, using the ORIGINAL provider contract from vendor/protocol-1.md (same contract \"count\" protocol \"1\" uses); protocol \"2\"/omitted uses the (account_id, delivery_id) identity with latest-wins, as before. Response shape is unchanged: exactly protocol, accepted_count, duplicate_count, receipts. The receipts array holds the accepted representative from each group, fields/payload/timestamp spelling unchanged, in ORIGINAL INPUT ORDER (not group order) -- achieved by filtering the original input list to the winning record_ids. accepted_count/duplicate_count for protocol \"1\" match \"count\" for an equivalent single-account request, and for protocol \"2\" match \"summary\" for an equivalent request. Empty input -> receipts [] and both counts zero; a single input receipt is always returned unchanged as the sole accepted representative, regardless of protocol.\n\nBasis: trial-adg issue description and vendor/protocol-1.md (protocol 1 original contract: delivery_id-alone identity, earliest-wins, smallest-record_id tie-break), trial-ewy issue description (protocol 2 identity contract), trial-tfh issue description (protocol 2 permanent adoption, integration-owner approval), trial-tau issue description (accepted command contract, original protocol-2-only scope, response shape, original-input-order requirement), and trial-hjc issue description (extending accepted to explicit protocol \"1\" using the original provider contract, same response shape, same original-input-order preservation). Implemented in main.py via a shared dedupe(receipts, key_fn, protocol) helper (latest_wins = protocol == \"2\") returning the winning (instant, record_id) per key; count/summary derive counts from it, and accepted() selects key_fn per protocol (delivery_id alone for \"1\", (account_id, delivery_id) for \"2\"/omitted) then filters the original receipts list by winning record_id to build the ordered receipts array. Verified via public test suites accepted_1 (new, protocol 1: empty and single-receipt cases) and accepted_2, plus a manual cross-account-same-delivery_id check confirming protocol \"1\" dedupes D-1 across accounts A and B while protocol \"2\" would keep them separate."
  },
